(contributing guides)

Do not use GitHub/GitLab pull/merge requests. I have enough
headache trying to deal with proprietary schemas already.
There is not a mailing list, and we can't use lists.sr.ht
since SourceHut probably hates me for using AI at all in
this project.  Email foss at rapidcow.org and I will update
the web site to "track" such changes.  I will publish a
monthly mbox (skipping months where I receive no mail) so
you should tell me if you want to be anonymized.

    N.B. While I don't like "pull request", you can still
         send me an email containing a "request to pull".
         Read git-request-pull(1) to find out how!

         Otherwise git-format-patch(1) is fine.  (diff -u
         is fine but only if the patch is small enough...)

Should you use your Internet domain name, use one that
you own or a name allocated to you by your e-mail provider
in the patches you submit.  I don't care if you can receive
at that address as long as it's yours.  Otherwise, mDNS
*.local is for myself, and you cannot use it unless you
are friend/family (though feel free to use any RFC 2606
top-level domains.)  You can always request to have your
mail corrected in .mailmap; getting names and mails right
is my gratitude to your contribution! :)  (Note that
correction does not equal redaction; people can and will
find your old name and email.  So pick carefully! o_o)

Also, regarding talk of the decade -- AI is okay provided
that *I* understand it.  If you can't convince me it is
a good idea, I probably don't want accept it.  You should
credit the *specific* AI model you use, such as "Claude
Sonnet 5" or "GPT-6 Astra".  I will make it so that your
patches, even if authored by AI, have you as the author,
and the AI model as the co-author.  (I am exempt from this
rule, but that doesn't mean you are!)

Lastly, respect my choices and my time.  I try not to
use up your time if it's something I can fix without
breaking a sweat, but if it's too much work for me I'll
have to ask you to improve it or not accept it at all...
To save as much time for yourself, try letting me see
your rough idea ASAP so I can see if it is a good idea!
instead of sending everything all at once after you are
done with it all...  (Again, if I don't understand it,
I unfortunately have to lump it into "AI slop". :<)
